ield/id #uuid "1f3a14a1-7676-561a-9298-96af99e9a3d3" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-2de4acfa-51aa-5671-b0d3-3dfe17c3742f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-57e2ee3c-9499-560b-ba1a-25d245e37439" "answer-2de4acfa-51aa-5671-b0d3-3dfe17c3742f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-57e2ee3c-9499-560b-ba1a-25d245e37439" :answer/id #uuid "57e2ee3c-9499-560b-ba1a-25d245e37439" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "dependent" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2de4acfa-51aa-5671-b0d3-3dfe17c3742f" :answer/id #uuid "2de4acfa-51aa-5671-b0d3-3dfe17c3742f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "independent" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-47c9e11d-3763-56a1-a6fd-21b1255f236b" :question/id #uuid "47c9e11d-3763-56a1-a6fd-21b1255f236b" :question/math-academy-id "q-334011" :question/problem "Given the set of functions ${\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\\,{e}^{x},\\,3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}$ defined on $x\\in R,$ select the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\nFor all $x\\in R,$ we have that\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+{{field-2}}\\cdot {e}^{x}+{{field-3}}\\cdot 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=0.\n$$\n\nSince \n{{field-4}} \nthe scalar coefficients in the linear combination are zero, the given set of functions is linearly \n{{field-5}}." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the set of functions ${{f}_{1}(x),{f}_{2}(x),…,{f}_{n}(x)},$ which are defined on some interval $I,$ is *linearly dependent* if there exist real scalars ${k}_{1},{k}_{2},…,{k}_{n}$ not all zero such that the linear combination ${k}_{1}\\cdot {f}_{1}+{k}_{2}\\cdot {f}_{2}+…+{k}_{n}\\cdot {f}_{n}$ is identically zero, i.e, \n\n$$\n{k}_{1}\\cdot {f}_{1}(x)+{k}_{2}\\cdot {f}_{2}(x)+…+{k}_{n}\\cdot {f}_{n}(x)=0\n$$\n\nfor all $x\\in I.$ Otherwise, if ${k}_{1}={k}_{2}=⋯={k}_{n}=0$ is the only solution, the set is *linearly independent*.\n\nNow, for all $x\\in R,$ we have that \n\n$$\n3\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+0\\cdot {e}^{x}+(-1)\\cdot 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=0.\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, since $\\text{not all}$ the scalar coefficients in the linear combination are zero, the given set of functions is linearly $\\text{dependent}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4b3ff0cc-2f32-5f3d-8c4a-1cfe74f94acc" "answer-field-cb37fa92-34ce-5da3-9cc2-7439e9823eb3" "answer-field-e75553da-6c04-50a4-a94c-aab86bb8cabd" "answer-field-77d6349d-b35a-5cd4-9174-8afd3686d64b" "answer-field-6bfcf71a-fd64-5c92-96e0-a4da19acec22"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4b3ff0cc-2f32-5f3d-8c4a-1cfe74f94acc" :answer-field/id #uuid "4b3ff0cc-2f32-5f3d-8c4a-1cfe74f94acc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-1918dcc5-9c9c-5d4c-8fb6-13ae3046b611" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d1c2bd37-d688-5185-bc0d-d9a7b5aa24e1" "answer-dff2af51-6b63-5e15-a1dd-5250c8ddde2a" "answer-1918dcc5-9c9c-5d4c-8fb6-13ae3046b611"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d1c2bd37-d688-5185-bc0d-d9a7b5aa24e1" :answer/id #uuid "d1c2bd37-d688-5185-bc0d-d9a7b5aa24e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dff2af51-6b63-5e15-a1dd-5250c8ddde2a" :answer/id #uuid "dff2af51-6b63-5e15-a1dd-5250c8ddde2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1918dcc5-9c9c-5d4c-8fb6-13ae3046b611" :answer/id #uuid "1918dcc5-9c9c-5d4c-8fb6-13ae3046b611" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cb37fa92-34ce-5da3-9cc2-7439e9823eb3" :answer-field/id #uuid "cb37fa92-34ce-5da3-9cc2-7439e9823eb3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-31b49dd0-7130-505e-8975-5b6b86b0fd97" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6f826a5b-626f-57ae-8de0-45b178d28a30" "answer-31b49dd0